## 4. Risk register

Likelihood and impact on a 1-3 scale; priority = likelihood x impact. Sections 5 and 6
follow this order.

| # | Risk | Type (product/project) | Likelihood | Impact | Priority | Mitigation | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | _(a failure a user or the business would notice)_ | product | 3 | 3 | 9 | _(test layer that catches it)_ | |

## 5. Test strategy

### 5.1 Risk-based prioritisation

_(how the register above turns into what is tested first and deepest)_

### 5.2 Test levels and the pyramid

| Level | Share | What it proves | Why this share |
|---|---|---|---|
| Unit | | | |
| Contract / API | | | |
| UI / end-to-end | | | |

### 5.3 Test types

_(functional, performance, accessibility, security, exploratory: which apply, and why)_

### 5.4 Test design techniques

_(equivalence classes, boundary values, state transitions, decision tables, pairwise)_

### 5.5 Test data

_(where data comes from, who owns it, how it is reset; synthetic vs masked production data)_

### 5.6 Test environments

_(which environments exist, what each is for, how close each is to production)_

### 5.7 Entry, exit and completion criteria

- **Entry:** _(build deployed, smoke green, data loaded)_
- **Exit:** _(all P1 risks covered and passing; open defects triaged)_

### 5.8 Retest and regression

_(what is rerun after a fix, and what runs on every change)_

### 5.9 Automation approach and tooling

_(what is automated, what stays manual, and the tools)_

### 5.10 CI/CD integration and quality gates

_(which suites gate a merge, which gate a release, and how long each may take)_

### 5.11 Defect management

_(severity vs priority, who triages, response times)_

### 5.12 Metrics

Each metric names the decision it drives. Raw test counts drive none.

| Metric | Decision it drives |
|---|---|
| Escaped defects per release | _(where coverage is missing)_ |
| Flaky-test rate | _(when to stop adding tests and fix the suite)_ |
| Gate duration | _(when to split or parallelise)_ |
| Risk coverage | _(whether the release is ready)_ |

